id: DRAFT-unpublished-test-dependency-blocks-upstream-tests
trigger_tool: conan|make|pkg-config
phase: dependency_resolution,testing
error_signature: Package libtheft was not found|theft.h: No such file or directory|Unable to find.*theft/0.4.5
severity: 3
category: build-system,dependency,testing,conan
match_keywords: skiparray,libtheft,theft,not published,test-only dependency,upstream tests,make,pkg-config,R36
title: Unpublished test-only Conan dependency blocks the upstream suite
root_cause: The production library builds without external packages, but its upstream test target requires theft/0.4.5 through pkg-config and theft.h; the exact test-only recipe is absent from the local cache and ohpcd, so the suite cannot compile in a clean OHOS environment.
affected_scope: C/C++ libraries whose optional upstream tests require a test-only Conan package that is not published in the target remote.
verification_cmd: conan install --build=never --requires=theft/0.4.5@ohpcd/stable; make CC=/data/service/hnp/bin/clang library; make CC=/data/service/hnp/bin/clang test
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: separate-production-build-from-unpublished-test-dependency
rec_description: Verify the missing exact dependency with build=never, build and package the independent production library with a real consumer test, and report the upstream suite as blocked. Publish the test dependency first before re-enabling the full upstream suite; never use build=missing, vendored copies, dummy packages, or print-only tests.
rec_command: conan install --build=never --requires=theft/0.4.5@ohpcd/stable; make CC=/data/service/hnp/bin/clang library; conan create . --build=skiparray/*
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: partial-package-with-consumer-evidence
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: publish-exact-test-dependency-then-rerun
fallback_description: REALIZED 2026-09-05 - theft/0.4.5 published on ohpcd (revision 46372da4dacaca771da48de53bf6661d); the exact test dependency was added only behind an upstream_tests recipe option, the upstream Greatest suite was rebuilt and rerun on device: 67 tests, 67 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (25 static RUN_TEST registrations expand to 67 parametrized cases); production default graph stays theft-free.
fallback_command: conan download theft/0.4.5 -r ohpcd --only-recipe; conan create . -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -o skiparray/*:upstream_tests=True --build=skiparray/* --build=theft/*
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: dependency-publication
forbid_1_pattern: build=missing.*theft|vendor.*theft|dummy.*theft
forbid_1_reason: A missing test dependency must be published in dependency order, not silently rebuilt or bundled into the consumer PR.
forbid_1_consequence: R36 is bypassed and clean CI cannot reproduce the claimed dependency boundary.
forbid_2_pattern: skip.*upstream|echo.*passed|print.*passed
forbid_2_reason: A blocked upstream suite is not a passing suite; a real consumer test is required for the package boundary but cannot replace the upstream result.
forbid_2_consequence: The PR overstates test coverage and hides the missing dependency.
forbid_3_pattern: test-only.*runtime|requires.*unpublished.*production
forbid_3_reason: Do not expose a test-only dependency as a production runtime requirement when the library itself is independent.
forbid_3_consequence: Consumers inherit an unavailable or unnecessary dependency and package resolution fails.
principles: P002,P003,P014
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to: E342,E458,E477
